{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-isic-0170"
 :itonami.blueprint/name "Hunting, Trapping And Related Service Activities Coordination"
 :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev5 "0170"
 :itonami.blueprint/domain :agriculture/hunting-trapping-services
 :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
 :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:food-security :conservation :wildlife-harvest-safety]
 :itonami.blueprint/governor :huntharvest-governor
 :itonami.blueprint/robotics false
 :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:identity :forms :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger :telemetry]
 :itonami.blueprint/optional-technologies []
 :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "`:huntharvest-governor` is implemented end-to-end in `src/huntharvest` as
 a WILDLIFE-HARVEST OPERATIONS COORDINATION actor -- HuntHarvest Advisor
 (LLM proposal-only) ⊣ Wildlife-Harvest Operations Governor (closed-op-
 allowlist / harvest-record-registration-before-any-action hard-gate /
 hunter-license-trap-inspection-trap-check-interval-trap-setback-quota-
 season hard-gates / unresolved-conservation-flag hard-gate / firearm-
 trap-deployment-and-licensing-authority permanent block).
 `:itonami.blueprint/robotics` is honestly `false` -- this actor holds NO
 firearm/trap-deployment control authority and NO wildlife-license-
 issuing authority (both are HARD, permanent governor blocks, never
 overridable by human approval -- see `huntharvest.governor` ns
 docstring). ISIC Rev.5 0170 covers COMMERCIAL/LICENSED wildlife
 harvesting for meat, pelts, or population-control purposes, and related
 service activities (e.g. game-ranching support services) -- this actor
 coordinates that work on behalf of an independently-verified harvest
 license and species quota allocation, it never deploys a firearm or trap
 itself and never issues or finalizes a wildlife harvest license. Every
 one of its four proposal ops (`:log-harvest-record` /
 `:schedule-harvest-operation` / `:flag-conservation-concern` /
 `:coordinate-shipment`) carries `:effect :propose` ONLY -- the governor
 HARD-holds any proposal that doesn't (`effect-not-propose-violations`).
 Harvest methods split into trap-based (leg-hold/live-cage trapping,
 carrying a genuine trap-check interval for humane treatment and a
 minimum trap setback distance for public safety) and direct-take
 (rifle/shotgun hunting, no trap to check or set back) -- the Governor's
 trap-specific checks are skipped entirely, never fabricated, for
 direct-take methods. Hunter/trapper license currency, species quota, and
 open-season windows apply to EVERY harvest method regardless of shape.
 `:flag-conservation-concern` always escalates to a human, at every
 phase, regardless of advisor confidence; `:coordinate-shipment` above a
 value threshold likewise always escalates. This build ships NO JVM-only
 interop anywhere in `src/` (all source is `.cljc`) per this workspace's
 cljs-first runtime-priority rule. See `README.md` for the full
 governor-check enumeration."}
